<title>UK: Eurotunnel shares restored after meeting.</title>
<headline>Eurotunnel shares restored after meeting.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Anglo-French channel tunnel operator Eurotunnel Plc said on Friday its shares had been restored after suspension on Thursday.</p>
<p>The company had requested temporary suspension of its shares ahead of a crucial meeting of shareholders on a bank debt restructuring deal.</p>
<p>Shareholders voted at the meeting in favour of the deal to slash the current shareholders' stake to 54.4 percent from 100 percent.</p>
<p>Eurotunnel shares were trading 1/2p higher at 82p in early dealings on the London stock exchange.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 4019</p>
